The API also serves completions, Responses and Anthropic Messages. /v1/models lists the served name.

To talk to a model in the terminal in one command, tensorfold chat MODEL starts the server itself, streams each
reply and stops the server when the chat ends; /help lists the chat's commands, and /bye or Ctrl-D ends it:



With the server above still running, tensorfold chat --url chats with it instead, and
 echo "Say hello." tensorfold chat --url prints one reply for a script.
See the chat command for its flags and the serve flags it passes on.

 Docs

- Run guide: platform setup, requests, parallel requests, exact decoding, context compaction,
 Cortheon mode, every serve flag, the Mac app and TensorFold Starlight.
- Supported models: which checkpoints run on which machines, models on disk and model discovery.
- Living Weights (experimental): teach a running model new facts in its own weights.
- Installation runbook: macOS and CUDA installation, paired Metal serving and troubleshooting.
- Windows, TensorFold Web and the Mac app.
- API, Cortheon mode and known issues.
- Evaluating TensorFold and community benchmarks.
- Usable memory profiles: how to record applied budgets, context, cache state and process peaks.
- Contributing: ATC and agents, builds, tests and the exactness and performance gates.
- Changes, 1.0.0 release notes and the Zig engine preview.
- TensorFold is Apache-2.0: LICENSE, NOTICE, THIRD PARTY NOTICES.md and SECURITY.md.

